{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790718605,"nonce":"YyHDkCLCAzGwrv4Y7Or+Ed45MqI=","title":"Drop insertion releases a conditionally transferred loop value twice","message":"Rust CI runs 36627130154 and 36631659382 fail after the loop-carried ownership changes. Linux and macOS fail `zyntax_lua --test capi` in `every_tier_calls_c_functions` and `values_c_holds_survive_constant_collection`. Windows aborts most Lua conformance groups with exit -1073740791 (0xC0000409).\n\nLocally, `ZYNTAX_BASELINE_THRESHOLD=1000000000 zylua run tiers.lua` aborts in `io_string_free`: `zl_print` frees a pointer whose string header has already been freed. Post-optimization HIR contains this shape:\n\n```\nacc = phi [seed, next]\nseparated = string_concat(acc, tab)   ; only on one arm\nselected = phi [separated, acc]\nnext = string_concat(selected, text)\nstring_free(selected)\nstring_free(acc)                      ; unconditional on the joined back edge\n```\n\nThe implicit back-edge use added for unread accumulator replacement is unnecessary when the old claim has a transfer edge into another owning phi. Normal liveness already sees the transfer and can release the old value on the non-transferring arm. Treating the joined back edge as another use inserts an unconditional second release on the transferring arm.\n\nRestrict the implicit replacement use to owning phis with no transfer edge. The resulting HIR frees `acc` on the separator arm, frees `selected` once after its final use, and carries `next` around the loop. Keep the implicit use for `x = make()` loops whose previous value is otherwise unread.\n\nValidation:\n\n- the focused conditional-phi regression fails under the old rule and passes with the restriction;\n- all 22 `drop_insert` unit tests pass;\n- all 3 Lua C API integration tests pass, including interpreter-only, baseline, default, LLVM-enabled, and forced-GC configurations;\n- the fixed interpreter-only `tiers.lua` output matches its pinned checksum.","files":null}]}